      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301175",
      ":question/problem": "A metropolitan area has $27,800$ registered cyclists. A random sample of cyclists was surveyed, and each participant was asked whether they plan to join a new city bike-share program. Of those surveyed, $42%$ responded that they plan to join.\n\nBased on this survey, which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of cyclists in the metropolitan area who plan to join the program?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
